.el .ds Aq '
.TH rev-stealth-hermes-uninstall 1  "rev-stealth-hermes-uninstall " 
.SH NAME
rev\-stealth\-hermes\-uninstall \- Remove a previously installed Hermes plugin
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrev\-stealth hermes uninstall\fR [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-explain\fR] [\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a previously installed Hermes plugin directory at <prefix> (default: $HOME/.hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp). No\-op if the directory is absent.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: side\-effect\-free plan emission. No file writes, no network calls, no keyring operations. Returns exit 0 after emitting the structured plan envelope
.TP
\fB\-\-explain\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5: include the action plan in the result envelope\*(Aqs `result.plan` field. Can be combined with `\-\-dry\-run`. When passed without `\-\-dry\-run`, the plan is emitted alongside the real action
.TP
\fB\-\-idempotency\-key\fR \fI<IDEMPOTENCY_KEY>\fR
v1.3 Lane G.5 / G.6: opaque caller\-supplied key for at\-most\-once commit semantics. Accepted in G.5; surfaced in the envelope; the underlying commit replay semantics land in G.6
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR
Plugin directory to remove. Defaults to `$HOME/.hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  $ rev\-stealth hermes uninstall
  $ rev\-stealth hermes uninstall \-\-prefix /opt/hermes/plugins/rev\-scraping\-mcp

EXIT CODES:
  0  Ok               Uninstall completed (or no\-op).
  1  UserError        Bad \-\-prefix.
  3  PermanentError   directory IO failure.

ENV:
  (none consumed directly; respects HOME for default \-\-prefix.)
